        body: "When turnaround is tight, writers default to safe language. Safe language reads as AI or as \"marketing.\"\n\nClients feel it too. They approve posts they don't love because revising feels slower than posting.\n\nThe fix isn't hiring more inspirational copywriters. It's building a workflow where voice, topics, and approvals happen before Thursday panic sets in.\n\nEach client should have a voice doc, example posts they like and hate, and clear boundaries on what needs legal or founder sign-off.\n\nTrack pushback themes per client. Three edits saying \"too salesy\" means update the voice doc, not just fix one post.",
